  "name": "24 HOURS URINE MICROALBUMIN",
  "code": "24 HOURS URINE MICROALBUMIN",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p style=\"text-align: start\">This test is often used to assess kidney function and to monitor the progress of certain kidney diseases, such as diabetic nephropathy.</p><p style=\"text-align: start\">Microalbuminuria is defined as the presence of small amounts of albumin in the urine that is not detectable by a routine urine test. The normal range for 24-hour urine microalbumin excretion is less than 30 mg/day. Values between 30-300 mg/day are considered to be indicative of microalbuminuria, while values over 300 mg/day indicate macroalbuminuria.</p><p style=\"text-align: start\">Microalbuminuria may be an early sign of kidney damage, particularly in people with diabetes or high blood pressure. If left untreated, microalbuminuria can progress to more serious kidney problems, such as chronic kidney disease.</p>",
